research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:1168:          "evidence": "Steps 2.1 and 3.1 establish that every solution of the normalized IVP equals exp."
research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:1173:    "thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation": {
research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:1314:          "evidence": "Step 1.1 derives F(0)=1 in the continuous case, and step 1.2 assumes and propagates the normalized value in the differentiable case."
research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:1869:          "evidence": "Step 4.1 differentiates the integral equation back to the normalized ODE."
research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:1914:          "source": "thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation",
research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:2917:          "claim": "If $F$ were continuous, [[thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation]] would give $F=\\exp$; injectivity of $\\exp$ would then give $A(x)=x$, contradicting $A(b)=0\\ne b$.   [step 1.1, step 2.1, L3, given]",
research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:2923:            "[thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation",
research/audit/wave14-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:2978:          "evidence": "Steps 3.1 and 4.1 use the normalized characterization contrapositively: if F were continuous it would equal exp, contradicting F(b)=1."
