research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6024-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6025-**Proof technique:** direct.
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6026-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6027-1.1 Termwise differentiation gives $(\exp)'(x)=\sum_{n\ge1}\iota(n)x^{n-1}/\iota(n!)$.  [L1, L2]
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6028-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6029-2.1 Reindex $n=j+1$ and cancel $\iota(j+1)$ using the factorial recurrence. The series becomes $\sum_{j\ge0}x^j/\iota(j!)=\exp(x)$.  [step 1.1, L2, algebra]
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6030-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6031-3.1 Smoothness follows from [L1] and the infinite radius; iterating step 2.1 gives every higher derivative.  [step 2.1, L1, L2] ∎
