research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6122-## Proof
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6123-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6124-**Proof technique:** direct.
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6125-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6126-1.1 Given a real $M$, every $x>\max\{0,M-1\}$ satisfies $\exp(x)\ge1+x>M$. Hence $\exp(x)\to+\infty$.  [L1, L3]
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6127-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6128-1.2 Given $\varepsilon>0$, choose $X>0$ with $1+X>1/\varepsilon$. If $x<-X$, then $-x>X$, so [L1] gives $\exp(-x)\ge1-x>1+X>1/\varepsilon$; [L2] yields $0<\exp(x)<\varepsilon$.  [L1, L2, choose]
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6129-
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-6130-2.1 The range assertions follow from positivity and the two limit conclusions.  [step 1.1, step 1.2, L2] ∎
